# DTF tier manifest: promotion-gate-results-and-origin
#   (artifact-keeper#4556, #4557, #4558, #3977, #4152, #4147, #4160, #1758)
# Profile-set: filesystem only. Every case is the promotion API, the scan
# policy / quality gate API, the artifact read API and Postgres; no scanner,
# no upstream and no signing key is involved. The audit's three Y2 tiers
# promotion-gate-results-and-metadata, bulk-promotion-gate-and-origin and
# promotion-warn-and-predicates share this profile set and are folded here.
#
# THE BUGS (all fixed in 1.11.0; RED image 1.10.0)
# #4556 / #4557: POST .../promote (single and bulk) reported only failures;
#   a passing promotion had no record of what was checked. 1.11.0 adds
#   gate_results[{rule,passed,reason}] to every PromotionResponse, including
#   a passed `policy-predicate` entry per predicate that held, its reason
#   carrying the policy name and the predicate token ([origin.kind],
#   [conda.license], ...). The conda-attestation facet of #4556 (a verified
#   CEP-27 bundle satisfying require_signature) belongs to the
#   conda-attestation-trust tier; this tier uses signature-free predicates.
# #4557: promotion inserted the target row and nothing else, so a promoted
#   conda package was served from the release channel with empty depends,
#   empty license and no md5. The copy now carries artifact_metadata. A
#   staging upload was stamped origin kind `virtual` (migration 284).
# #4152: the copy's origin was derived from the TARGET repository; it now
#   carries the source's origin document verbatim.
# #4558: two scan policies with the same name on one repository were
#   accepted; now 409 (case-insensitive), create and rename.
# #3977: bulk promotion never ran the quality gate or the policy, a `warn`
#   gate's violations were dropped from every success response, and bulk
#   promotion_history.policy_result was a {"passed":true} placeholder.
# #4147 / #4160: the promotion gate never evaluated scan_policies.predicates
#   (origin and conda); the conda channel allowlist fails closed on a package
#   whose identity records no channel.
# #1758: artifact GET and listing responses carry last_promotion
#   {target_repo_key, promoted_at, status}; null when never promoted (or only
#   refused); target_repo_key null for a caller who cannot read the target.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   generic staging repos with: no gate (control), an origin.allowed_kinds
#   [hosted] policy (passes), [proxy] (refuses), a warn quality gate and a
#   block quality gate (min_health_score 50 against the computed score 0 of a
#   generic file); conda staging repos with conda.denied_licenses (passes),
#   conda.allowed_channels [conda-forge] (refuses) and an allowlist naming
#   the repository itself on a package whose identity purl had its channel
#   qualifier removed in Postgres (the "channel unknown" state).
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) on both images: an ungated promotion copies the bytes, the
#             target serves them, one history row; a block gate refuses a
#             SINGLE promotion with 409 naming the gate; a same-named policy
#             on another repository is accepted.
#   (FIX)     every other case; on 1.10.0 the response has no gate_results,
#             predicates are inert, bulk ignores gates and policies, warn
#             violations are [], artifacts.origin and last_promotion do not
#             exist, and the release repodata loses depends/license/md5.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: about 80 authenticated calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
